  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "OAI Provider does not conform to the Open Archives Interface.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The OAI Provider in Fedora does not conform to the Interface in",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "several respects: First of the Date the objects are filtered by is",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "CreationDate and NOT LastModification date.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "from",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/openarchivesprotocol.html#Datestamp:"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/openarchivesprotocol.html#Datestamp:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"Harvesters may use datestamps to harvest only those records that were",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "created, deleted, or modified within a specified date range.\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Which isn't possible because filtering is done on CreationDate. This",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "problem was reported before (",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-716#icft=FCREPO-716"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": "), but the bugfix was not applied.",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "Furthermore the datestamp published in the OAI headers was also the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "creationDate which of course should be LastModificationDate.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The earliestDatestamp in the Identify answer is also wrong. In the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "class FedoraOAIProvider, The earliestDatestamp is created by a call to",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "new Date(), so everytime you ask for the earliestDatestamp you would",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "just get now.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "from",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/openarchivesprotocol.html#Identify:"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/openarchivesprotocol.html#Identify:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"earliestDatestamp : a UTCdatetime that is the guaranteed lower limit",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "of all datestamps recording changes, modifications, or deletions in",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "the repository. A repository must not use datestamps lower than the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "one specified by the content of the earliestDatestamp",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "element. earliestDatestamp must be expressed at the finest granularity",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "supported by the repository.\"",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Which in no way is supported by the current implementation.  I've",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "supplied a patch which I believe addresses these issues.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The \"Best\" earliest timestamp can be found through a rather heavy",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "fieldsearch search, but instead I've used the idea in the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "FedoraOAIProvider which adds a 'dcmDate>'2001-01-01'\" to fieldsearch",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "searches. I've defined an earliestDate field (set to 2001-01-01),",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "which is used as the earliestDatestamp value in the Identify answer,",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "and this value is also used to restrict the fieldsearch querys.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We would really like this patch to be applied, and, if for some",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "reason, the patch does not address certain important issues, please",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "respond so I can create a patch that everybody is happy with.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
